-allow-policy","l":"full","t":"Redrive allow policy","x":[]},{"a":[],"id":"sqs.dlq.redrive-task","l":"limited","t":"Dead-letter queue redrive tasks (StartMessageMoveTask)","x":["A redrive task runs to completion immediately (moving every available message) instead of a real, rate-limited background task — Status is always COMPLETED, so there is no RUNNING task to track progress on or cancel with CancelMessageMoveTask, and MaxNumberOfMessagesPerSecond is accepted but has no effect."]},{"a":[],"id":"sqs.sns-subscriptions","l":"full","t":"SNS subscriptions (subscribe/unsubscribe this queue to an SNS topic)","x":[]},{"a":[],"id":"sqs.lambda-triggers","l":"limited","t":"Lambda triggers (event source mappings)","x":["A message landing in the queue is invoked synchronously, one message per Lambda invocation, the instant SendMessage returns — not through a real batched, asynchronous poller. BatchSize / MaximumBatchingWindowInSeconds are stored but have no effect on batching. The message is deleted from the queue only if the invocation succeeds (LastProcessingResult reflects the real outcome); a function error leaves it for redelivery, same as real SQS."]},{"a":[],"id":"sqs.eventbridge-pipes","l":"limited","t":"EventBridge Pipes (queue as a pipe source)","x":["A message is forwarded to the pipe's Target the instant SendMessage returns, not through a real background poller. Enrichment and InputTemplate/filtering on the pipe are stored but not applied — the raw message body is forwarded as-is. The message is removed from the source queue only once delivery to a real target (an existing queue/topic/function/state machine/stream) succeeds."]},{"a":["GetMetricStatistics"],"id":"sqs.queue.metrics","l":"limited","t":"Historical CloudWatch metrics","x":["Published to CloudWatch (AWS/SQS, dimension QueueName) from real queue activity as it happens: NumberOfMessagesSent/Received/Deleted, SentMessageSize, NumberOfEmptyReceives (counters) and the Approximate*Visible/NotVisible/Delayed + AgeOfOldestMessage gauges recomputed from the queue's contents whenever they change. There is no 1-minute publish schedule, so a gauge only has points when the queue changed."]}],"id":"sqs","ops":21,"registry_unreachable":[],"title":"Simple Queue Service","total":23}
